WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.963
Here's what you'll be able to
do by the end of this module.

2
00:00:02.963 --> 00:00:06.348
You'll name the least-privileged
roles that read Service Health,

3
00:00:06.348 --> 00:00:09.287
and the one a security advisory's
sensitive fields need.

4
00:00:09.287 --> 00:00:12.524
You'll compare the kit's events
query with Learn's samples.

5
00:00:12.524 --> 00:00:17.575
You'll collect the fixture subscriptions
and read each event's kind and action date.

6
00:00:17.575 --> 00:00:21.155
And you'll plan Service Health
alerts at scale with Azure Policy,

7
00:00:21.155 --> 00:00:23.925
and show that fixture mode
never applies the plan.

8
00:00:23.925 --> 00:00:27.600
You need Module 1, for the
record and its action basis.

9
00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:33.024
If you have time, read the Azure platform
and Microsoft 365 audit telemetry chapter

10
00:00:33.024 --> 00:00:35.540
of Security Operations and Telemetry,

11
00:00:35.540 --> 00:00:40.650
which sends the Azure activity log's
Service Health category to the workspace.

12
00:00:40.650 --> 00:00:44.812
Lab 1 needs PowerShell 7.1
or later with Pester 5.

13
00:00:44.812 --> 00:00:45.790
No tenant.
